        "original_id": "fa92d555-f808-5f81-9ef1-5af0e0218e38",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Independent Commission on the Voting System, Jenkins Commission\n- People: Roy Jenkins\n- Systems: Alternative Vote Plus, United Kingdom electoral system\n- Places: United Kingdom\n\nFacts:\n- Roy Harris Jenkins, Baron Jenkins of Hillhead, was born on 11 November 1920 and died on 5 January 2003.\n- Roy Jenkins was a British politician associated with the Labour Party, SDP, and Liberal Democrat party, and he was also a biographer of British political leaders.\n- The Independent Commission on the Voting System was popularly known as the Jenkins Commission after its chairman Roy Jenkins.\n- The Jenkins Commission examined possible reform of the United Kingdom electoral system.\n- In 1998, the Jenkins Commission devised Alternative Vote Plus and first proposed it as a system for elections to the Parliament of the United Kingdom.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
